    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d84">

                <pb facs="0246" n="150" sameAs="frus:frus1898/pg150"/>

                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Baron Riedl to Mr.
                            Hay.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Imperial and Royal Austro-Hungarian Legation</hi>,<lb/><hi
                                rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1899-01-17"><hi rendition="#italic">January
                                17, 1899</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Dear Mr. Secretary of State</hi>: Referring to our
                    last conversation on the Lattimer affair, I have the honor to inform you that
                    Mr. Robert D. Coxe is free to proceed to Washington January 18, 19, 20, 21,23,
                    and 28.</p>
                <p>You would very much oblige me by having me informed which of the days aforesaid
                    and what hour would be convenient to you for granting the favor of an audience
                    to Mr. Coxe.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Riedl.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
